text:
What is the best thing in the world?

June roses pearled by May dew;

The sweet south wind saying there will be no rain;

Truth, with friends stripped of cruelty;

Beauty, not made vain until its pride is spent;

Love, when we are loved again.

What is the best thing in the world?

Something outside it, I think.

